From a5a65f82fce6c374ecbdb6d06f690414163b1843 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 17:58:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] add libyaml's licence next to the package's own
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream-Status: To upstream [development happens in Mercurial on SourceForge and the ruamel/yaml.clib GitHub mirror states pull requests are ignored and deleted, so submitting this needs a SourceForge ticket]

The extension statically compiles the bundled libyaml sources (api.c,
emitter.c, parser.c, reader.c, scanner.c, writer.c, loader.c, dumper.c and
their headers, closest to libyaml 0.2.2). Those are MIT-licensed by Ingy
döt Net and Kirill Simonov, whose licence requires the copyright notice to
travel with binary redistributions, but the built wheel ships only
ruamel.yaml.clib's own LICENSE.

Adding the file is enough on its own: setuptools' default license_files
glob (LICEN[CS]E*) picks it up, so it lands in the wheel's
dist-info/licenses/ next to LICENSE with no packaging change.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.libyaml | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.libyaml

diff --git a/LICENSE.libyaml b/LICENSE.libyaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e8f8805
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.libyaml
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
